      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "SHARNI'S SECRET (5) was strongly supported last start when a short priced favourite and duly saluted winning by 2.5 lengths at this track in a handy 20.20. Has a tricky draw to overcome but in form and has the ability. Makes plenty of appeal on the back of that last-start win. LUCKY HARPER (2) is yet to miss the placings in an excellent record this track and trip which boasts two wins and two placings. Comes off a (20.41) win last time, scoring by 1.5 lengths in a Grade 5 over 350m at this track. Can feature in the finish. DR. PATRICK (1) was safely held last time out, finishing sixth at Sale over 435m behind Dr. Tessa (25.27) in a Grade 5. Better than the latest run and deserves another chance. HYPNOTIZING (8) is always hard to beat when drawn in this box.",
